{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795852947,"nonce":"uz79+EUFj5HbPwtq5WiBPlV4ehs=","title":"Flaky: unverified_email_owner_entry_does_not_grant_owner fails when the stub IdP's key generation outlasts the login timeout","message":"Seen once on CI, 2026-11-28, run 46121444386 (job test-and-coverage, PR #236). The same test passed on the previous run of the same branch and passes on main; nothing on the branch touches the login path.\n\nSymptom: crates/scarab-server/tests/oauth_flow.rs:394, body_json: called Result::unwrap() on an Err value: Error(\"expected value\", line: 1, column: 1). The response being parsed is POST /v1/auth/login, which answers plain text 401 \"authentication required\" when the code exchange fails.\n\nLikely cause (from reading, not reproduced; the server-side log line was not available):\n- The stub identity provider's /token handler calls sign_id_token, which calls keys() (tests/oauth_flow.rs ~50-65). The first call generates two RSA-2048 keys in a debug build inside OnceLock::get_or_init, on a tokio worker thread, while the server under test waits for that response.\n- The server's reqwest client has a 30 s total timeout (src/oauth.rs ~333).\n- nextest runs each test in its own process, so every test pays the key generation. Under coverage instrumentation and a loaded runner it can exceed the timeout; the exchange fails and login answers 401.\n\nFix (test harness only):\n- Generate the keys in provider() before it returns, so the cost is outside the server's timeout; or embed a fixed test key pair.\n- Make api_login / body_json assert the status and print the body, so the next failure names its cause.\n\nThe suite stops at the first failure, so one flake hides every later test in that run.\n\nRelated closed flakes under load: ed819bd, 789ed54.","files":null}]}